WEBVTT

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.110
Fuuman Plain

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.780
Commanding General of Gi

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.250
So someone got here before me.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.790
Commanding General of Gi

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.000
I am Go Hou Mei, commanding general of Gi.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.250
You're young.
I'm En's commanding general, Ordo.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.450
Ordo? From the tribe
of horsemen in the north?

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:47.200
So? Why are you sitting in the center?

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.450
No reason. First come, first served, that's all.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:07.500
The party's already getting started, I see!

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.500
Commanding General of So

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.950
Commanding general of So, Kan Mei.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.620
Oho! Been a while since I've seen
a man bigger than me.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.250
That giant is Kan Mei.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.450
And of all people, Kan sends...

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.350
Commanding General of Kan

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.330
Sei Kai, commanding general of Kan.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:29.910
Gentlemen?

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:32.830
That should be everyone.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.500
The Battle of Kankoku Pass

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.790
What is that man doing in a place like this?

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:23.120
Especially when Kan Mei
is here as So's general.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:29.250
This is exactly what gets my blood pumping.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:35.700
The great generals of each nation,
coming together when normally we'd clash.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.660
Apart from Se, that is.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.450
Oh, forget them!

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.620
Ri Boku.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:48.660
I am positively delighted
to be able to fight with you.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:55.080
Yes, to fight you, my greatest enemy,
once the coalition army has disbanded.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:04:00.120
I'm grateful that En has joined
the coalition army.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.120
I understood you talked
the King of En into it, Ordo.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.250
Because it's <i>you</i> .

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:10.160
With your overwhelming victories
over Chin's Ou Ki and En's own Geki Shin,

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:15.120
the eyes of the entire Middle Kingdom
are now on you, Ri Boku.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.910
This coalition army only came together
because <i>you</i> , and no other, reached out to us.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:27.410
Why, I suspect Geki Shin may have been
sacrificed for this very cause.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.620
Never mind that.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.950
What would bring someone like <i>you</i> to this place?

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.450
In this coalition, there is no high or low.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.700
All member armies are on an equal footing.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.000
However,

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.950
being an army, it will require someone
to bring you all together.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.750
Of course.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:53.830
Hmm?

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.620
So that's how it is.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.040
Yes.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.370
So chancellor and their army's high commander:

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.290
Shun Shin Kun.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.910
So Chancellor and 
High Commander

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:07.700
He will serve as the commanding
general of our coalition army.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:14.580
The last of the Four Lords of the Warring States,
with some 3,000 hangers-on...

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.790
In his 20 years as chancellor,

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:20.370
he brought all of the vast land
of So together as one.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:25.160
If you were to rank all in the Middle Kingdom,
both civil servants and military men,

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:28.040
he would come out on top.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.910
So our general <i>isn't</i> Ri Boku?!

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:34.200
Worry not, Ordo.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:39.870
From start to finish,
the man directing this war is my staff officer,

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.910
Ri Boku.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:46.870
My role is simply to kick your asses into gear.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.830
Any other objections?

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:56.620
Though I've made the north my stomping grounds,
I do know of Shun Shin Kun.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.330
Could our line-up be any more magnificent?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:05.080
This coalition army is the best, all right!

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.450
Things are taking shape.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:10.160
Now we need a strategy, Ri Boku.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:17.910
I'll go over our plan for capturing Kanyou.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.040
With Chin's manpower,

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.580
we have no means of stopping
the coalition army invasion.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.660
None at all.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:30.790
Therefore, we will do away with
the many layered lines of defense

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.700
between them and Kanyou.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.160
Do away with them?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.540
We can't have pointless battles
widening the gap in our manpower.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:46.660
Soldiers and townsfolk will wait in nearby
castles for the coalition army to pass.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.200
Are you <i>trying</i> to get them to Kanyou?

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.750
Just to the entrance.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.040
The entrance?

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.000
Ha! You former mountain bandits
don't know anything.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.330
Say what?

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:03.700
Surrounded by mountains,
Kanyou is a natural stronghold.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:09.120
Another reason Kanyou is called
the Middle Kingdom's most impregnable castle

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:14.200
is the national gate that blocks
the one road leading to its door.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.580
That much I know.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:20.580
This gate has never once been breached.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:26.620
But we've never been under siege
like this before, either.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.910
Exactly right.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.830
So we tighten up the gate as usual.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:43.830
Correct. Defending Kanyou
comes down to only one thing:

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:48.410
how to keep that gate at
its entrance safe through it all.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:50.120
Easy enough to understand.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.700
It's all we can do.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:59.290
Then I'd ask each of you to
assemble your armies at once.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.500
To the gate at Kankoku Pass!

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.910
Check it out, gang! More Chin troops!

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.500
And more further in!

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.540
They're heading to Kanyou.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.870
No, they're off to the Kankoku Pass gate.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.330
It's not far ahead.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:23.160
Rumor is almost all the armies
are comin' together.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.660
How 'bout the Gaku Ka Force
and the Gyoku Hou Force?

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.040
What the--

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:37.660
"Chin"

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.410
Are they <i>all</i> allies?

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.000
There are just so <i>many</i> of them!

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.330
Maybe this is their rendezvous point?

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.330
Huh?

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:49.040
It's... it's <i>massive</i> !

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.410
This must be...

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.910
...Kankoku Pass!

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.660
I can't even see the top!

00:08:56.660 --> 00:09:00.450
How many dozens of years
did it take to build this thing?

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:05.370
Even the castle wall at Kanyou
is only half as high.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.500
Twice as tall as the wall
around the royal capital?!

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:12.620
Hooray! Three cheers for Kankoku Pass!

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:35.550
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:18.950
Ten...

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:25.250
They say if anyone gets past Kankoku Pass,
Kanyou is done for.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.660
It's true.

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:28.870
Huh.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:33.750
Come on, there's no way
<i>anyone</i> could get past <i>that</i> !

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.790
Ri Boku's on his way 'cause he's sure <i>he</i> can.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:38.790
Ri Boku...

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:44.580
We ain't defendin' Kanyou.
We're defendin' Kankoku Pass!

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.450
Get into position, Hi Shin Force!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.060
"Hi"

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.060
Kanyou

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:53.660
Apologies, Mou Bu.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:58.040
With your location,
you'll probably see the most bloodshed.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.500
Just what I like to hear.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:06.040
Still, this is an uncharacteristic
miss on your part.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.450
A coalition army...

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:11.410
Never thought you'd let
that slip this far past you.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.540
I'm to blame. I didn't take them seriously.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:22.330
I never thought anyone would guess
the real reason behind the Sanyou Offensive.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.370
The Middle Kingdom, in checkmate?

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.160
Yes--with that one move.

